      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n\n## Column Mapping\n- academic year: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- academic year description: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\n- coefficient of variation of the total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- Mathematics subjects: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- fall term: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM\n- total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- range of the number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- variance of the number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE <-> SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"math\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each academic year, give the academic year description and the coefficient of variation of the total units for subjects offered in that year, considering only subjects that are offered in the fall term, have more than zero total units, and are in the Mathematics department (Course 18).\n```sql\nSELECT ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, STDDEV_SAMP(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS) / AVG(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS) AS coefficient_of_variation FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ccso JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL ata ON ccso.TERM_CODE = ata.TERM_CODE WHERE ccso.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND ccso.IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM = 'Y' AND ccso.TOTAL_UNITS > 0 GROUP BY ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC ORDER BY ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR;\n```\n2. For each academic year, what is the range and variance of the number of enrolled students in courses, considering only courses that are offered in the fall term, have more than zero enrolled students, and are offered by the Mathematics department (Course 18)? Show the academic year and these two statistics.\n```sql\nSELECT ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR, MAX(TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) - MIN(TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_range, VARIANCE(TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_variance FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS ON COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE = ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE JOIN TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED ON ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE WHERE COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM = 'Y' AND TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' GROUP BY ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR ORDER BY enrolled_range DESC;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each academic year, show the academic year, academic year description, the coefficient of variation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for Mathematics subjects offered in the fall term with more than zero total units, the range of the number of enrolled students in Mathematics courses offered in the fall term with more than zero enrolled students, and the variance of the number of enrolled students in those courses. Do not return any rounded answers."
