      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database remains inaccessible (persistent authentication error `1045 Access denied`), so live data verification is not possible. I will finalize based on the complete semantic-network evidence and the gold decomposition. Below is the full report.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables**\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: catalog-level attributes per subject offering per term/academic year. Key columns: `TERM_CODE`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME` ('Mathematics'), `TOTAL_UNITS`, `IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM` ('Y'/'N'), `SUBJECT_ID`, `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`. The only offering table with full catalog attributes (units + offering flags).\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL**: extended term dimension (superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS). Carries `TERM_CODE`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`; lacks `IS_REGULAR_TERM`/`TERM_STATUS`/`ADD_DATE`/`DROP_DATE`.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS**: status-tracked term dimension subset. Carries `TERM_CODE`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`, plus `IS_REGULAR_TERM`, `TERM_STATUS`, `TERM_STATUS_INDICATOR`.\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: textbook-program subject offerings, one row per subject per term; carries `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `TERM_CODE`, `IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL`.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED**: section-level registrar offerings; has `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` and `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` at section grain, but **no unit columns** (per concept comparison matrix).\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY**: subject-level rollup with `TOTAL_UNITS` and `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`; no offering-term flags.\n- **SUBJECT_SUMMARY**: subject/cluster-level final enrollment statistics with `TOTAL_UNITS`, `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER`; no `IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM` flag.\n- **LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: library-reserve-scope subjects with `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`; program-scoped snapshot.\n- **CIS_COURSE_CATALOG / DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG**: alternative catalog feeds with the same attribute structure (units, `IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`) from CIS/Drupal sources.\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT**: department dimension (code, name, full name, school, degree-granting flag).\n- **TIP_DETAIL**: TIP material rows per subject/term (material status, ISBN, record count).\n\n**Metrics (precedents)**: dw_2180 (CV of TOTAL_UNITS per academic year with ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC — `STDDEV_SAMP/AVG` over SUBJECT_SUMMARY⋈ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL), dw_4640 (CV of NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS — `STDDEV/NULLIF(AVG,0)` over TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED), dw_1023 (Math fall-term unit variance/STDDEV per academic year over COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED⋈ACADEMIC_TERMS with `IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM='Y'`), dw_41 (Math yearly avg/variance of TOTAL_UNITS via ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL⋈COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED), dw_4701 (yearly ACADEMIC_YEAR/ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC + fall-term unit stats), dw_3417 (yearly AVG/STDDEV of TOTAL_UNITS), dw_1335, dw_2958 (yearly VARIANCE/STDDEV of NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS via SUBJECT_OFFERED⋈ACADEMIC_TERMS), dw_1288, dw_1350 (range = MAX−MIN and VARIANCE of TIP NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS), dw_1165 (enrolled_range/enrolled_variance over TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED), dw_2272, dw_2158, dw_2377, dw_1301, dw_4229 (COURSE_CATALOG⋈ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL⋈TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED on TERM_CODE with `IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM='Y'` and `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS>0` — exact same join shape as required here), dw_1212, dw_1049.\n\n**Concepts**: concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_academic_term_dimension, concept_course_catalog_sources, concept_course_material_programs, concept_department_dimension (details in Sections 2–4).\n\n**Column Concepts**: column_concept_term_code, column_concept_year_columns, column_concept_total_units, column_concept_enrollment_measures, column_concept_department_name, column_concept_subject_id.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- Join keys (from column_concept_term_code and gold hints): `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE ↔ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE`; `ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE ↔ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE`; `ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE ↔ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE`; `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE ↔ SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE`. TERM_CODE is the universal fact↔dimension join key.\n- concept_subject_offering_facts groups all six offering fact tables; concept_academic_term_dimension groups ACADEMIC_TERMS / ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL / ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER; concept_course_catalog_sources groups the three catalog feeds; concept_course_material_programs links TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED → TIP_DETAIL; concept_department_dimension groups SIS_DEPARTMENT / STUDENT_DEPARTMENT / SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT.\n- Metric lineage: dw_1023, dw_41, dw_4701, dw_3417, dw_2158, dw_2377, dw_1301, dw_4229 all consume COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED + a term table; dw_2180 consumes SUBJECT_SUMMARY + ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL; dw_4640, dw_1350, dw_1165 consume TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix** (evidence: concept_subject_offering_facts comparisons, column concepts):\n\n| Dimension | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED | SUBJECT_OFFERED | SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY | SUBJECT_SUMMARY | TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED | ACADEMIC_TERMS | ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | subject offering/term (catalog) | section/term | subject/term | subject or cluster/term | subject/term (TIP scope) | term | term (superset) |\n| TOTAL_UNITS | yes (catalog-declared) | **no unit columns** | yes | yes | **none** | n/a | n/a |\n| IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM | **yes** | no | no | no | no | no | no |\n| NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | none | yes (section) | yes (subject) | no (SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER) | **yes** | n/a | n/a |\n| ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC | no | no | no | no | no | yes | yes |\n| Coverage | catalog offerings | all sections | all subjects | all subjects | TIP program scope only | status-tracked subset | all terms |\n| Fan-out risk | — | section duplication | — | cluster rows | term-only joins fan out (precedent dw_4229 accepts this) | — | — |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness Mapping** — atomic requirements: (R1) measure TOTAL_UNITS; (R2) filter `IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM='Y'`; (R3) filter `DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics'`; (R4) group key ACADEMIC_YEAR + ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC; (R5) measure NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS with >0 filter; (R6) CV = STDDEV/AVG, range = MAX−MIN, variance = VARIANCE.\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: R1 SUPPORTED, R2 SUPPORTED (only table with the flag), R3 SUPPORTED (DEPARTMENT_NAME per column_concept_department_name), R4 via TERM_CODE join, R5 NOT-SUPPORTED (no enrollment).\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED: R5 SUPPORTED (NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS), R1/R2 NOT-SUPPORTED (no units, no fall flag) — must pair with catalog table.\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED: R1 NOT-SUPPORTED (no units), R2 NOT-SUPPORTED → cannot serve either measure set alone.\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY: R1 SUPPORTED, R2 NOT-SUPPORTED (no fall flag) → violates R2.\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL: R4 SUPPORTED (widest coverage; decision_guide: \"source of academic year, academic year description … over the widest term coverage\"). ACADEMIC_TERMS: R4 SUPPORTED (subset coverage).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring**: \"offered in the fall term\" lexically matches only `IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM` (catalog tables); \"total units\" → `TOTAL_UNITS` (gold mapping: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS); \"Mathematics subjects / Course 18\" → `DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics'` (domain knowledge hint); \"number of enrolled students\" → gold mapping pins `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (not SUBJECT_OFFERED's); \"academic year description\" → `ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`, present in both term tables — gold mapping pins ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL for the CV branch and ACADEMIC_TERMS for the enrollment branch, matching precedents dw_41/dw_2180 (ALL) and dw_1023/dw_2958 (TERMS).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence**: CV-of-TOTAL_UNITS per year: 2 precedents — dw_2180 (SUBJECT_SUMMARY⋈ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, `STDDEV_SAMP/NULLIF(AVG,0)`) and the gold decomposition (COURSE_CATALOG⋈ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL). Math fall-term unit stats on COURSE_CATALOG: dw_1023, dw_41, dw_4701, dw_3417 (4 precedents). Enrollment range/variance on TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS: dw_1350, dw_1165, dw_4640 (CV form) — 3 precedents. TERM_CODE-only three-way join COURSE_CATALOG⋈term⋈TIP with fall + enrolled>0 filters: dw_4229 (exact same shape).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: default source for unit statistics and offering-flag filters (decision_guide of concept_course_catalog_sources and column_concept_total_units); consumed by dw_1023, dw_41, dw_2158, dw_2377, dw_1301, dw_4229, dw_4701.\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED: enrollment snapshots within textbook-program scope; consumed by dw_4640, dw_1350, dw_1165, dw_1288, dw_4229.\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL / ACADEMIC_TERMS: year enrichment; ALL used for widest coverage year/desc sourcing, TERMS when status/regular flags needed (dw_1023, dw_2958, dw_3417).\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS/DRUPAL catalogs, SIS_DEPARTMENT, TIP_DETAIL: serve other question shapes (section grain, official enrollment, reserve scope, alternative feeds, department attributes, material counts) — not needed for this task's measures per the gold column mapping.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nAll Phase 1 entities investigated: tables COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, ACADEMIC_TERMS, ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG, SIS_DEPARTMENT, TIP_DETAIL (semantic_get); metrics dw_2180, dw_4640, dw_1023, dw_4701, dw_41, dw_3417, dw_1335, dw_2958, dw_1288, dw_1350, dw_1165, dw_2272, dw_2158, dw_2377, dw_1301, dw_4229, dw_1212, dw_1049 (semantic_get with full SQL); concepts concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_academic_term_dimension, concept_course_catalog_sources, concept_course_material_programs, concept_department_dimension (semantic_get); column concepts column_concept_term_code, column_concept_year_columns, column_concept_total_units, column_concept_enrollment_measures, column_concept_department_name, column_concept_subject_id (semantic_get). mysql_query attempted 4 times — all failed with `1045 Access denied` (environment issue, noted explicitly).\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (`TOTAL_UNITS`, `IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `TERM_CODE`) for the CV branch joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (`ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`); use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (`NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, `TERM_CODE`) joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS and COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED for the enrollment branch; combine the two per-year aggregates on ACADEMIC_YEAR.\n\n**6b.** Two CTEs (each single-level aggregated per academic year), then an inner join on ACADEMIC_YEAR, ordered by academic year. CV = `STDDEV(TOTAL_UNITS)/AVG(TOTAL_UNITS)` — per the mandatory tip, bare `STDDEV()` is written even though the question says \"using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP\". Range = `MAX−MIN`, variance = `VARIANCE()`. Filters exactly as decomposed: `DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics'`, `IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM='Y'`, `TOTAL_UNITS>0`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS>0`. The enrollment branch joins on TERM_CODE only (fan-out is intentional and matches precedent dw_4229 and the gold decomposition). SELECT list: exactly 5 columns — academic year, academic year description, CV, range, variance.\n\n**6c.** *Data*: only COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED physically has both TOTAL_UNITS and IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM (column definitions retrieved); only TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED has NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS per the gold mapping; ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL gives the widest year/desc coverage. *Semantic-network*: column_concept_total_units decision_guide (\"unit statistics over catalog offerings → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\"); concept_academic_term_dimension decision_guide (ALL for year/desc sourcing); column_concept_enrollment_measures (TIP scope enrollment). *Business*: dw_1023/dw_41/dw_4229 precedents use the identical table/join/filter shapes; dw_1350/dw_1165 establish MAX−MIN + VARIANCE on TIP enrollment.\n\n**6d.** Alternative: SUBJECT_SUMMARY-based CV (dw_2180 precedent) — rejected because it lacks the fall-term flag required by the question and contradicts the gold column mapping. STDDEV_SAMP vs bare STDDEV: the system tip mandates bare `STDDEV()`, which is followed here. Database verification was impossible due to the persistent access-denied error; the SQL is syntactically standard MySQL 8 (CTEs supported per precedent metric SQL).\n\n",
